===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|rót|root}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*wrōts}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*wrd-||root}}; compare with English {{m|en|wort}} and the Latin {{m|la|rādīx||root}}. Cognate with the Faroese {{m|fo|rót}}; Old English {{m|ang|rōt}} (whence the Middle English word {{m|enm|root||the underground part of a plant}} came, whence the English {{m|en|root}} came).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/rouːt/|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|ouːt|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|rótar|rætur}}

